    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Lord Cornwallis introduced the Permanent Settlement in Bengal, Bihar, and Orissa in 1793, creating a class of hereditary Zamindars.",
        "The Ryotwari System was implemented by Thomas Munro and Alexander Reed in Southern and Western India, directly linking the state with cultivators.",
        "The Mahalwari System was formulated by Holt Mackenzie and introduced in North-Western Provinces, establishing revenue units based on village communities (Mahals).",
        "Administrative reforms under Cornwallis established a professional Indian Civil Service and separated executive from judicial functions via the Cornwallis Code.",
        "The Charter Act of 1853 replaced patronage with an open competitive examination system for recruitment to the Covenanted Civil Services."
      ],
      "id": "13t5upo"
    },
