    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Permanent Settlement (1793) covered ~19% of British India, assigning permanent land ownership rights to Zamindars.",
        "Ryotwari system covered ~51% of British India and involved periodic re-assessment of revenue directly with peasants.",
        "Cornwallis Code of 1793 separated revenue collection from judicial administration.",
        "Charter Act of 1853 introduced open competitive exams for the Civil Services, ending the patronage system."
